  "what_this_is": "The green pointer versions at sequences 1-9, reconstructed from the operations records that registered each move by hand. It is NOT a copy of any stored object: those versions were overwritten before the durable promotion history existed, and their bytes are gone from araripe-v2-staging.",
  "never_written_to_the_store": "By design (docs/implementation/PHASE_6C_2026-09-27.md §2.4). The store's history means one thing only - a byte-exact copy of an accepted pointer write - and its keys are write-once, so a reconstruction placed there would occupy the original's key forever and could never be corrected. A reconstruction is a claim derived from documents, and claims live where they are reviewed: here, by pull request.",
  "how_it_is_checked": "Against the store at the one point where the two speak: the supersedes of the first stored record (sequence 10) names the release, sequence and coverage of the last entry here. src/publication/retention.py build_lineage refuses the reconstruction otherwise. And tests/test_retention.py reads every document and section cited below and requires the full release id and the sequence to appear there.",
  "used_by": "the green retention planner only (scripts/plan_retention.py). Never by publication, never by the delivery route.",
